# Series DOCX publication

When building or restyling any Practical Engineering Word file, follow `SERIES-PUBLICATION-STYLE.md` and import colors from `tools/docx/series_style.py`. Do not invent a new palette.

Required treatment:

- Author is `Birol Tilki` on the title page and in document properties.
- First published edition of every book is `v1.0`. Title line: `Version 1.0`. Filenames: `practical-<book>-engineering-v1.0.docx` and `.pdf`.
- Contents omits How to Use This Book. List numbers match chapter numbers. Put the number inside the hyperlink text. Wrap the heading text with the bookmark.
- Running header is the numbered chapter title only. Do not put the book name in the header.
- Table header cells: `#D9D9D9`. Body rows alternate `#FFFFFF` and `#E8E8E8`. Borders: `#4B5563`. No blue-gray fills.
- Two-column tables are equal width. Bold the After column only in Before/After tables.
- Practice boxes: `#EAF4FF` with a `#2E74B5` left bar.
- Source Code paragraphs: `#F2F2F2` (Gray-5%).

Apply this to every future series DOCX (SRE, Platform Engineering, and later books), not only DevOps and DevSecOps.
